WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.233
In the 1930s, Adolf Hitler became the leader of Germany.

2
00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:11.576
He was a very evil man and committed many horrible crimes against the people of Europe.

3
00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:20.633
In 1940, he attacked the peaceful nation of Holland.

4
00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:25.926
The people of Holland, called the Dutch, were forced to become part of Germany.

5
00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:32.313
They had to live under German law and do whatever the German soldiers told them to do.

6
00:00:32.314 --> 00:00:40.140
If the German soldiers wanted their food or blankets, they had to give them up.

7
00:00:40.141 --> 00:00:45.669
After the Germans defeated the Dutch, the queen of Holland had to leave the country.

8
00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:50.753
Queen Wilhelmina , her daughter, and granddaughters all escaped to

9
00:00:50.754 --> 00:00:53.718
London. But London was not very safe

10
00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:59.071
either. Hitler and his army were bombing London every

11
00:00:59.072 --> 00:01:08.573
night. So, Queen Wilhelmina sent her daughter, Princess Juliana, and her granddaughters to live in Ottawa, the capital city of

12
00:01:08.574 --> 00:01:18.398
Canada. In Ottawa, the Canadian people took very good care of the princess and her

13
00:01:18.399 --> 00:01:22.469
daughters. However, Queen Wilhelmina did not come to

14
00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:26.770
Canada. Even though it was very dangerous, she stayed in

15
00:01:26.771 --> 00:01:30.297
London. She would send radio messages to the people of

16
00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:33.724
Holland. She would tell them not to give

17
00:01:33.725 --> 00:01:37.770
up. In Ottawa, Princess Juliana had a baby

18
00:01:37.771 --> 00:01:44.022
girl. To celebrate, the Canadians raised the Dutch flag and played the Dutch national

19
00:01:44.023 --> 00:01:51.227
anthem. It was a wonderful feeling for the

20
00:01:51.228 --> 00:01:57.596
princess. The queen heard about the celebration and announced the exciting news on her radio broadcast.

21
00:01:57.597 --> 00:02:05.371
When the people of Holland heard this news, they were very thankful to the Canadians.

22
00:02:05.372 --> 00:02:12.786
Then, in 1944, the Canadian soldiers came to Holland and helped defeat the German army.

23
00:02:12.787 --> 00:02:16.751
The people of Holland were even more grateful for this.

24
00:02:16.752 --> 00:02:27.153
The people wanted to thank the Canadians for taking care of their princess and for helping defeat Hitler's army.

25
00:02:27.154 --> 00:02:33.446
Princess Juliana presented the city of Ottawa with 100,000 tulip bulbs.

26
00:02:33.447 --> 00:02:36.894
Holland is famous for its beautiful tulips.

27
00:02:36.895 --> 00:02:40.143
The country is covered with tulips every spring.

28
00:02:40.144 --> 00:02:47.363
So, the gift of tulips to Canada was a true sign of friendship.

29
00:02:47.364 --> 00:02:52.050
Tulips grow in the early spring and then die just before summer.

30
00:02:52.051 --> 00:02:54.761
But the tulip bulbs do not die.

31
00:02:54.762 --> 00:02:56.613
They stay in the earth.

32
00:02:56.614 --> 00:03:03.349
Every spring they blossom into beautiful new tulips again.

33
00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:08.682
Every year, the Queen of Holland sends 10,000 more tulips to Ottawa.

34
00:03:08.683 --> 00:03:14.696
Now, after more than fifty years of sending them, Ottawa is full of tulips.

35
00:03:14.697 --> 00:03:22.559
Every spring, Ottawa celebrates with a festival.

36
00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:27.676
The Canadian Tulip Festival is the largest tulip festival in the world.

37
00:03:27.677 --> 00:03:37.872
The city of Ottawa is not only the capital city of Canada, it is also the capital city of tulips.

38
00:03:37.873 --> 00:03:46.038
Princess Juliana, who became Queen Juliana, attended the tulip festival during a royal visit in 1967.

39
00:03:46.039 --> 00:03:58.960
The tulips in Ottawa have become a beautiful sign of the friendship between these two countries.

